<p>Your online store is at <code>yourshop.hardpoint.app/store</code>. Customers browse, see what's in stock at your branches, and order for
  collection. There's nothing to build.</p>

<h2>Switching it on</h2>
<ol>
  <li>The owner goes to <strong>Settings › Online store</strong>.</li>
  <li>Tick <strong>Online store is on</strong>, choose the branches customers can collect from, and add a headline, a few words about the shop and
    when orders are ready (for example "Orders before 3pm are ready the same day").</li>
  <li>Choose whether customers see how many are in stock, or only "In stock", "Low stock" and "Out of stock".</li>
</ol>
<p>Every active product with a price is in the store. To keep one out, open the product and untick <strong>Show in the online store</strong>.
  Photos you add to products appear in the store.</p>

<h2>When an order comes in</h2>
<ul>
  <li>It appears in <strong>Sales › Orders</strong> marked <strong>Online</strong>, and owners and managers get an email.</li>
  <li>Pack it, then press <strong>Mark ready and text</strong>: the customer gets a text and their order page shows it's ready.</li>
  <li>When they come, ring the order up at the till as usual. Anything they paid ahead by M-Pesa is already on the order as a deposit.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Paying ahead</h2>
<p>If you've connected an M-Pesa Paybill, the customer's order page shows your business number with their order number as the account number.
  Payments made that way are matched to the order automatically. Till (Buy Goods) numbers can't carry an order number, so with one of those
  customers pay when they collect.</p>
